          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "4.2",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "5ab830dfaea9dd514f340c91d24d5e9774beb5d7498096f26e0cad7eae9b98a7",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0003",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 4.2,
              "timestamp": "2026-07-26 03:37:45 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/Tool-Calling/.github/workflows/",
              "cwe": "CWE-829",
              "impact": "If an attacker compromises a GitHub Action repository or if the action maintainer's account is taken over, the mutable @v4 reference could be updated to point to a malicious version, enabling code execution in the CI/CD pipeline with repository write permissions.",
              "technical_analysis": "Three GitHub Actions workflow files use mutable tag references:\n\n1. `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` - uses `actions/checkout@v4`, `actions/setup-node@v4`, `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3`, `actions/deploy-pages@v3`\n2. `.github/workflows/sync-stars.yml` - uses `actions/checkout@v4`, `actions/setup-node@v4`\n3. `.github/workflows/trending-weekly.yml` - uses `actions/checkout@v4`, `actions/setup-node@v4`\n\nThese mutable references can be silently repointed by the action owners, enabling supply-chain attacks. The recommended practice is to pin references to full 40-character commit SHAs.",
              "remediation_steps": "Pin all GitHub Action references to their full 40-character commit SHA instead of mutable tags. For example, change actions/checkout@v4 to actions/checkout@b4ffde65f16936253d0b0a9c6d5a3e8e7c1d2f3a. Use tools like renovate bot or dependabot with the sha pinning option to automate this process.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Review .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml for mutable action references.\n2. Observe that actions/checkout@v4 and actions/setup-node@v4 are used without SHA pinning.\n3. Verify that these tags can be moved by action maintainers, unlike fixed commit SHAs.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        }
